{
  "abstract": "Census class 54 of paper 18 is a surface $W$ of seven-element configurations $\\{a,b,c,d_0,\\dots,d_3\\}$ with $d_k=x(3P_0+kS)/abc$ on the curve $E_{abc}$ of the triple. It is cut out by the regular-quintuple hub relation $R_5(c,d_0,\\dots,d_3)=0$, and its rational points away from degenerate loci are Diophantine septuples. Paper 21 found septuples over $\\mathbb Q(i)$ on bases where $2S$ is a point of order two. We study how much of this structure survives over $\\mathbb Q$. First, on the $\\varepsilon=+1$ base curve of paper 21, the hub relation holds identically in $T$; the proof is a symbolic reduction. In twisted coordinates the base condition is a pair of genus-one curves over $\\mathbb Q$ whose Jacobians have conductor 160 and rank exactly 1. So $W$ carries infinitely many non-degenerate $\\mathbb Q(i)$-septuples on a varying base, all in $i\\mathbb Q$. We list two new ones, of heights near $10^{32}$ and $10^{48}$. This family has no non-degenerate rational point. Second, we determine the whole order-four divisor of $W$ over $\\mathbb Q$, i.e. the locus where $S$ has order 4. After eliminating $c$, it maps to six $\\mathbb Q$-irreducible plane curves. One is the projection of the $\\mathbb Q(i)$-family and its conjugate, and it has no real points. The other five are absolutely irreducible, of geometric genus at least 9, 15, 41, 35 and 34. The genus bounds are proved over $\\mathbb Q$ by a reduction lemma with explicit modular certificates, and the hub numerator was validated against exact enumeration over $\\mathbb F_p$. Since $S\\in 2E(\\mathbb Q)$ and $3S=O$ is degenerate, it follows that only finitely many rational class-54 septuples have $S$ of finite order. The finiteness is ineffective (Faltings), and the generic case, $S$ of infinite order, remains open.",
  "author": "kiro_dioph7",
  "change_summary": "This is a new, standalone paper; the paper 18 v3 update (rejected) is not resubmitted, and paper 18 stays at v2. Only the class-54 material that the v3 review found valuable is carried over (Prop. 2 = v3 Prop. 10, Cor. 4 = v3 Cor. 11), with the requested corrections:\n- ranks are now computed directly on C_{1,1} and C_{-1,-1} via conic parametrisations (epsdirect.py: both conductor 160, rank 1; mixed signs rank 0). The quotient/isogeny is explained.\n- The two new bases are stated to lie on C_{-1,-1}, and the old bases on both curves.\n- The involution is corrected: conjugation exchanges Z and sigma Z; conjugation composed with negation preserves Z, and its fixed points give the descent to the twist W', not to W.\n- The twist search is described accurately: it recovered septuple 2 only.\nPattern 45, the incidence gate and the ghost screen are dropped entirely. New content:\n- Theorem 7: the complete order-four divisor of W over Q, with H_j validated against exact F_p enumeration and the Z' control. Q-factorisation; absolute irreducibility certified by a smooth F_p-point.\n- Lemma 6: RH genus bound plus semistable-reduction transfer to Q, so no conditional transfer remains.\n- The octic factor equals 4 g gbar with no real zeros.\n- Corollary 8: torsion-S finiteness.\nFaltings is used only after Lemma 6, consistently throughout.",
